# Lines tools/pi-run's check must see, in this order, as whole serial lines
# (the Pi 5 only, systems/rpi5b_2gb/gem-net-test.system): the NIC
# driver releases the PHY's reset, identifies and resets RP1's GEM MAC, finds
# the PHY on MDIO and restarts auto-negotiation - having first looped one
# frame back inside the MAC (loopback_local) through its DMA and both rings,
# with no link; the stack takes its seed
# and asks for a lease. What the LAN gives - the link's speed and duplex,
# the lease's address - differs from desk to desk, so it is printed
# ("link up at ...", "DHCP lease ...") but not checked here; on the desk's
# LAN the lease comes within seconds of the link, and the stack answers ping. The run lasts
# its run length, 180 s, for a ping from the LAN.
NOWAYOS: timer: starting
NOWAYOS: gem-net: starting
NOWAYOS: gem-net: PHY reset released (the firmware held it); waiting 50 ms
NOWAYOS: gem-net: GEM_GXL revision 0x0109, design 0x08820000; it sees memory at bus address physical + 0x1000000000
NOWAYOS: gem-net: MAC reset; receive and transmit off, rings empty
NOWAYOS: gem-net: self-test: a 60-byte frame looped back through the MAC's DMA and rings, byte for byte
NOWAYOS: gem-net: PHY at MDIO address 1, identifier 600d:84a2 (model 0x0a, revision 2)
# The link is rgmii-id: the PHY delays both RGMII clocks. It starts with its
# transmit delay on and its receive skew off; with the skew off the MAC
# receives nothing. Then one frame through the PHY's loopback, over
# the RGMII bus both ways.
NOWAYOS: gem-net: PHY's RGMII delays for rgmii-id: receive skew on (was off), transmit delay on (was on); shadows 0x73e7 0x0e00
NOWAYOS: gem-net: self-test: a 60-byte frame looped back through the PHY at 1000 Mb/s, byte for byte
NOWAYOS: gem-net: auto-negotiation restarted: 10, 100 and 1000 Mb/s advertised
NOWAYOS: gem-net: ready, MAC 52:54:00:12:34:56: waiting for a link
NOWAYOS: net-stack-test seed_source: starting
NOWAYOS: net-stack-test seed_source: a fixed test seed sent on the stack's seed ring
NOWAYOS: net-stack: starting
NOWAYOS: net-stack: seeded; interface up at 52:54:00:12:34:56: asking for a DHCP lease
# The run's end: after its 180 s the ticker stops, and the PM
# watchdog resets the board.
NOWAYOS: watchdog-stand-in: ticker: the run length is reached: no more ticks, so the watchdog services no more and the board resets

# Output that fails the run at once: a fault, a kernel error, a panic, the
# driver giving up or failing to follow the link, the stack not ready or
# losing its lease, a queue or ring error.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!following the link
!the PHY's registers
!not ready
!a seed refused
!lease lost
!could not
!queue:
!ring:
!not looped back
!RGMII delays:
